{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And you shall love.</b> Do His words out of love — one who acts out of love is not like one who acts out of fear: one who serves his master out of fear, once the master lays a burden on him, he leaves him and goes his way (ibid.)." "<b>With all your heart.</b> With both your inclinations (Sifrei; Berakhot 54); another matter — <b>with all your heart</b>: that your heart not be divided against the Omnipresent (Sifrei)." "<b>And with all your soul.</b> Even if He takes your soul (Sifrei; Berakhot 54)." "<b>And with all your might.</b> With all your property — there is a person whose property is dearer to him than his body (Bereshit Rabbah 57); therefore it says בְּכָל מְאֹדֶךָ. Another interpretation — <b>and with all your might</b>: in every measure that He measures out to you, whether a measure of good or a measure of punishment — and so David says (Psalms 116) ״כוֹס יְשׁוּעוֹת אֶשָּׂא צָרָה וְיָגוֹן אֶמְצָא״ וגו׳ (cf. Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:11.257598148Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}